<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2><div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para"><p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure<math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\,\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\,\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where<math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies, for <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p><table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table"><tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V(x)\preceq\beta I\,,\hskip 20.00003ptx\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\kappa\coloneqq\tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V(x)\preceq\beta I\,,\hskip 20.00003ptx\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\kappa\coloneqq\tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td><td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1.1)</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The main result of this paper is the following.</p></div>
